    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The World as an Artwork",
      "links": [],
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Lewis Carroll",
      "links": [],
      "level": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "“That’s another thing we’ve learned from your Nation,” said Mein Herr, “map-making. But we’ve\ncarried it much further than you. What do you consider the largest map that would be really useful?”",
      "links": [],
      "level": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "“About six inches to the mile.”",
      "links": [],
      "level": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "“Only six inches!” exclaimed\nMein Herr. “We very soon got to six yards to\nthe mile. Then we tried a hundred yards to the mile.\nAnd then came the grandest idea of all! We actually made a\nmap of the country, on the scale of a mile to the mile!”",
      "links": [],
      "level": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "”Have you used it much?” I enquired.",
      "links": [],
      "level": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "“It has never been spread out, yet,”\nsaid Mein Herr: “the farmers objected: they said it would\ncover the whole country, and shut out the sunlight! So we\nnow use the country itself, as its own map, and I assure you\nit does nearly as well.\"",
      "links": [],
      "level": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sylvie and Bruno Concluded,\n1893 [Chapter\nXI: The Man in the Moon.]",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Chapter XI: The Man in the Moon.",
          "href": "http://www.hoboes.com/html/FireBlade/Carroll/Sylvie/Concluded/Chapter11.html",
          "external": true
        }
      ]
    },
